> \]”

*Correct.*  After fixing the vertical lines \(x=1,\dots ,x=n-k\), the uncovered points are precisely those with \(x>n-k\).  Translating \(x' = x-(n-k)\) yields the set \(T_k\) as described.

---

### 4.  Bounding the number of points a sunny line can contain in \(T_k\)

> “Multiplying its equation by a common denominator we obtain an integer equation  
> \[
> p x-q y=c ,\qquad \gcd(p,q)=1,\;q>0,\;p\neq0,\;p\neq -q .
