> “*Even \(k\).*  Write \(k=2m\;(m\ge1)\).  Then the left‑hand side of (3.2) equals \(2m\cdot m=m(2m)=k^{2}/2\), whereas the right‑hand side equals \(m(2m+1)=k^{2}/2+m\).  Because \(m>0\), (3.2) is false.  Hence **no even \(k\ge2\) is possible**.  
